# sia-lab admin-auth fixes — prepared 2026-10-19 ~13:35 +06, NOT yet applied or deployed.
# The main agent is mid-thread with Redowan in the side chat about the TMDB key /
# admin password being wiped on every update. Apply on the next deploy (he is
# about to pick a permanent password; the deploy that locks it in should carry this).
#
# DIAGNOSIS
# 1) Every deploy wipes ALL Durable Object storage. worker.js:1109 calls
#    env.TUNNEL_DO.idFromName("main-v28") and the name is bumped on every deploy
#    (main-v2 -> ... -> main-v17 -> ... -> main-v28). idFromName() maps each
#    unique name to a FRESH, EMPTY Durable Object, so each deploy orphans:
#      admin_pw, tmdb_key, meta:* (all movie posters/info), ext:* (all external links)
#    This is the entire "password/TMDB key reset on every update" saga, and it
#    also silently deletes his movie metadata + external links each time.
#    FIX: freeze the name (comment added below). The deployed DO right now IS
#    "main-v28" (deployed 2026-10-19 ~07:23 UTC), so freezing keeps everything
#    he set today (TMDB key at ~13:26 local, external links, metadata).
#    Worker secrets are NOT needed for the key/password once the name is frozen.
# 2) /api/admin/upload (PUT) and /api/admin/buckets (POST/DELETE) compare the
#    password against env.ADMIN_PW directly — but deploy_worker.py sets NO
#    secrets/vars, so env.ADMIN_PW is undefined and these endpoints ALWAYS 403,
#    for any password. Admin file uploads and shelf add/delete are broken right
#    now (independent of the wipe issue). The 2.83 GB MKV failure was diagnosed
#    as the 100 MB Cloudflare cap, but every admin upload also hits this 403.
#    FIX: use the checkPw() helper like every other admin endpoint does.
#
# HOW TO APPLY: cd ~/workspace/sia-lab && patch -p1 < fix-admin-auth.patch
# then deploy with deploy_worker.py as usual. No DO migration needed.
# Optional later cleanup: rename the DO to a stable "main" with a one-time
# copy of storage from "main-v28" — only cosmetic, do NOT do it casually.

